&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;
		&lt;ol&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;What is this PR for?&lt;br/&gt;
    Display form input has a `ng-enter` catcher, so if you use SHIFT + ENTER, the run function will be called twice.&lt;br/&gt;
    This PR is resolving the issue by removing the `ng-enter`, making the display form input react to SHIT + ENTER only.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;/ol&gt;
		&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;
		&lt;ol&gt;
